===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/fɑːl/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-farl.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɑːl|s=1}}

===Etymology 1===
Contraction of {{m|en|fardel}}, probably with some influence from the Irish {{m|ga|fearann}} meaning a fourth, especially of land or oatcakes. In this specific sense, fearann itself may be a possible cognate from a Norse or Old English root.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|obsolete}} A quarter of a thin oatmeal or flour cake.
# Any such cake or bread, now especially an Irish speciality such as a [[soda farl]] or [[potato farl]].

